BOUNDED CONCLUSION
k=pi/4: LATE_TIME_LINEAR_INSTABILITY_DETECTED — PHYSICAL IDENTITY UNRESOLVED
k=pi/2: NO_MODE_PLATEAU_WITHIN_TESTED_TIME
The positive linear instability meets the declared numerical rolling-slope,
contamination, noise-floor, and amplitude-linearity rules. Half-amplitude
agreement and small even/odd contamination establish linearity. The t=8
background drift and explosively growing linearized constraint response
prevent identification as a GL mode. There is no tested late-time negative
endpoint, so no k_cr*r0 bracket, asymptotic rate, physical-boundary
acceptance, or conclusion about whether k_cr*r0 is above or below 0.75
follows. The k scan remains suspended.
